---
// cut-the-mouse-cannot-make — the central idea of the β-MSH page. Both humans
// and rodents cut POMC into ACTH and β-lipotropin, and both cut ACTH down to
// α-MSH. In humans, prohormone convertase 2 then cuts β-lipotropin to
// γ-lipotropin and β-endorphin, and γ-lipotropin at a pair of basic residues
// to release β-MSH. Rodent POMC lacks that dibasic site, so processing stops
// at γ-lipotropin and no β-MSH is made. Schematic; SVG-only, wrap in <Figure>.
---

<svg
  class="ctm-fig"
  viewBox="0 0 640 318"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="ctm-t ctm-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="ctm-t">The cut the mouse cannot make: how β-MSH is released from POMC in humans but not rodents</title>
  <desc id="ctm-d"
    >Two rows compare POMC processing. In both humans and rodents, POMC is cut
    into an N-terminal fragment, ACTH and β-lipotropin, and ACTH is cut further
    to α-MSH. In the human row, β-lipotropin is cut to γ-lipotropin and
    β-endorphin, and γ-lipotropin is cut at a pair of basic residues to release
    β-MSH, a 22-amino-acid peptide. In the rodent row the same steps occur, but
    γ-lipotropin has no dibasic cut site, so processing stops there and no
    β-MSH is produced.</desc
  >

  <!-- ===== HUMAN ROW ===== -->
  <text x="20" y="30" class="row">Human</text>
  <!-- POMC bar -->
  <rect class="seg" x="20" y="42" width="110" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="75" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">N-terminal</text>
  <rect class="seg" x="136" y="42" width="130" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="201" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">ACTH</text>
  <rect class="seg lph" x="272" y="42" width="348" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="446" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">β-lipotropin</text>
  <text x="20" y="84" class="sub">POMC, cut at pairs of basic residues by prohormone convertases</text>

  <!-- ACTH → α-MSH (shared) -->
  <path class="cut" d="M201 66 L201 100" />
  <polygon class="cut-arrow" points="196,92 206,92 201,100" />
  <rect class="seg out" x="156" y="100" width="90" height="22" rx="6" />
  <text x="201" y="115" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">α-MSH</text>

  <!-- β-LPH → γ-LPH + β-endorphin -->
  <path class="cut" d="M446 66 L446 100" />
  <polygon class="cut-arrow" points="441,92 451,92 446,100" />
  <rect class="seg lph" x="272" y="100" width="190" height="22" rx="6" />
  <text x="367" y="115" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">γ-lipotropin</text>
  <rect class="seg" x="468" y="100" width="152" height="22" rx="6" />
  <text x="544" y="115" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">β-endorphin</text>

  <!-- γ-LPH → β-MSH (human only) -->
  <path class="cut hot" d="M367 122 L367 156" />
  <polygon class="cut-arrow hot" points="362,148 372,148 367,156" />
  <text x="378" y="142" class="mini hot-t">a pair of basic residues · the cut site</text>
  <rect class="seg hot" x="312" y="156" width="110" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="367" y="172" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t hot-t">β-MSH</text>
  <text x="430" y="172" class="tag">22 amino acids · a second ligand for MC4R</text>

  <!-- divider -->
  <line class="divider" x1="20" y1="200" x2="620" y2="200" />

  <!-- ===== RODENT ROW ===== -->
  <text x="20" y="226" class="row">Mouse &amp; rat <tspan class="sub">— after the same first cuts</tspan></text>
  <rect class="seg" x="20" y="238" width="110" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="75" y="254" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">N-terminal</text>
  <rect class="seg" x="136" y="238" width="130" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="201" y="254" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">ACTH</text>
  <rect class="seg lph" x="272" y="238" width="190" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="367" y="254" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">γ-lipotropin</text>
  <rect class="seg" x="468" y="238" width="152" height="24" rx="6" />
  <text x="544" y="254" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">β-endorphin</text>

  <!-- α-MSH still made -->
  <path class="cut" d="M201 262 L201 284" />
  <polygon class="cut-arrow" points="196,276 206,276 201,284" />
  <text x="201" y="302" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t">α-MSH — made as usual</text>

  <!-- no cut at γ-LPH -->
  <line class="nocut" x1="357" y1="262" x2="377" y2="284" />
  <line class="nocut" x1="377" y1="262" x2="357" y2="284" />
  <text x="367" y="302" text-anchor="middle" class="seg-t dim-t">no dibasic site · no β-MSH</text>
</svg>

